  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>isdatetime</keyword>
  <short_description>Test whether an input is a datetime array.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>tf = isdatetime(A)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>inputs</param_name>
      <param_description>Any Nelson value.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>output</param_name>
      <param_description>A logical scalar.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p>Test whether an input is a datetime array.</p>
    <p>Use isdatetime to branch on datetime support before calling datetime-specific functions such as datenum, dateshift, tzoffset, or isnat.</p>
    <p>Array-valued inputs keep their data shape when the operation supports arrays. Scalar operands are expanded where the implementation defines scalar expansion.</p>
  </description>
  <used_function />
